  <h2>What SessionSeal is</h2>
  <p>
    SessionSeal seals your master, stems, and session file into a
    cryptographically signed, timestamped record, and can later link copies
    of your track back to that record.
  </p>

  <h2>What a record proves, and what it doesn't</h2>
  <p>
    A sealed record proves <strong>custody</strong> (you held these files),
    <strong>integrity</strong> (they haven't changed since sealing),
    <strong>coherence</strong> (they plausibly belong together), and
    <strong>priority</strong> (you had them at a certain time). It
    <strong>never proves authorship</strong>. A record is evidence, not a
    verdict: we make no promise about how any court, platform, or dispute
    process will weigh it, and nothing here is legal advice.
  </p>

